ecreational boaters use the bay to access nearby state marine parks and federal cabins.","wpu":"Passage Canal","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Passage_Canal-Chugach.jpg/960px-Passage_Canal-Chugach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Whittier is a city at the head of the Passage Canal in the Chugach Census Area in the Unorganized Borough of Alaska, about 58 miles (93 km) southeast of Anchorage. The city is located within the Chugach Census Area, established in 2019 when the former Valdez–Cordova Census Area was dissolved. The city's population was 272 at the 2020 census, having increased from 220 in 2010.","wpu":"Whittier, Alaska","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Whittier%2C_Alaska_aerial_view_2026.jpg/960px-Whittier%2C_Alaska_aerial_view_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}